  "case": "MariaDB EMPTY_STRING_IS_NULL preserves empty ENUM labels and SQL NULL through CSV import",
  "test": "enum_sql_mode_contract::value_contract_mariadb_empty_enum_label_csv_restore_survives_empty_string_is_null",
  "engine": "MariaDB 11 Docker integration fixture",
  "outcome": "Pass",
  "contract": [
    "The source ENUM contains an empty label, the literal label NULL, and SQL NULL; native ordinal, HEX, and IS NULL oracles distinguish all three.",
    "With EMPTY_STRING_IS_NULL enabled in the pool session, the CSV importer reconstructs an empty ENUM label using CASE WHEN ? = 1 THEN SPACE(0) ELSE ? END, so no empty-string parameter is bound.",
    "After import, native ordinal and label bytes exactly match the source, SQL NULL stays NULL, and the existing sibling row is unchanged.",
    "Before the fix, the focused case failed because the empty label was restored as SQL NULL; the baseline failure is recorded."
  ],
